{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers","id":1183967,"title":"Two New Daggers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-09T09:25:13-08:00","id":1183967,"title":"Two New Daggers","content":"Tricky one, this one! Hard to come up with some categories to vote between, and I'm feeling lazy, so... an open vote! You can post up an idea, or post your vote for someone else's idea. Top two ideas get a dagger write-up each. However, I will exercise the power of NO to suggestions that are too naff, annoying, awkward or boring, and generally you're better off going with a looser request or idea than a more specific one, as it'll give me a bit more freedom when it comes to the actual write-up.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo... come up with ideas, and vote! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T09:28:32-08:00","id":1183969,"title":"","content":"Well this whole Christmas table has a sore lack of Idigam and I heard they're the chef's specialty? <br /> So... <br /> A knife themed/associated Idigam or something like that I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T09:39:06-08:00","id":1183975,"title":"","content":"I have two, but they are sort of similar.<br /> <br /> One is inspired by a hint in the Toothcracker's write-up during Five Pounds of Meat. Simply, a dagger crafted from the tooth or claw of a Firstborn. Given freely, fallen, pried from the corpse of some ancient Shadow-Colossus or whatever. Could be a Forsaken or Pure Firstborn, or even one of the briefly mentioned ones in Sundered World or one never mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> The second is similar in vein, and sort of inspired by the HAST/'Ur' write-up in the same day. It occurred to me that we know what omphalos stones are to mages but we don't know what they do for werewolves, if anything (and unofficially, even). Regardless, it's a dagger crafted from a part of a Pangaean's husk, or empowered by (or carved from) an omphalos stone. I'd actually prefer it if the Pangaean was linked to one of the hosts, if possible, even if it's an unofficial one like the Ukusgualu, but any is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T09:43:05-08:00","id":1183976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1183975#post1183975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two, but they are sort of similar.<br /> <br /> One is inspired by a hint in the Toothcracker's write-up during Five Pounds of Meat. Simply, a dagger crafted from the tooth or claw of a Firstborn. Given freely, fallen, pried from the corpse of some ancient Shadow-Colossus or whatever. Could be a Forsaken or Pure Firstborn, or even one of the briefly mentioned ones in Sundered World or one never mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> The second is similar in vein, and sort of inspired by the HAST/'Ur' write-up in the same day. It occurred to me that we know what omphalos stones are to mages but we don't know what they do for werewolves, if anything (and unofficially, even). Regardless, it's a dagger crafted from a part of a Pangaean's husk, or empowered by (or carved from) an omphalos stone. I'd actually prefer it if the Pangaean was linked to one of the hosts, if possible, even if it's an unofficial one like the Ukusgualu, but any is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Second The dagger made from an Pangaean idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T09:55:27-08:00","id":1183980,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a dagger which is associated with the theme of eclipses, in one way or another? I don't know, when I think about which dagger to suggest, I can only see a blade with the colours of black, white, silver and gold, with a half black sun drawing and I keep seeing the words &quot;forged by the moon, to cut the sun&quot;.<br /> <br /> Damn synesthesia, what can I say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:13:11-08:00","id":1183990,"title":"","content":"A idigam would be pretty awesome.<br /> Maybe about knives or blades in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:15:22-08:00","id":1183991,"title":"","content":"<br /> Idigam and a knife made from a firstborn tooth sound great to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:20:13-08:00","id":1183993,"title":"","content":"I'd like to propose:<br /> <br /> A dagger crafted from a shard of the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T10:25:00-08:00","id":1183997,"title":"","content":"Mine's more a modification to existing ideas: The Two either are designed to work together, or strangely have some additional, unintensioned (side-)effect when used so.<br /> <br /> If that is beyond the scope of the vote... count mine toward an Idigam Knife (moon-bound or earth-bound).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T11:34:29-08:00","id":1184023,"title":"","content":"A dagger made as a ritual implement rather than as a weapon would be neat, possibly as a specification for the above eclipse-themed or Gauntlet-shard knives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T12:09:19-08:00","id":1184034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1183975#post1183975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two, but they are sort of similar.<br /> <br /> One is inspired by a hint in the Toothcracker's write-up during Five Pounds of Meat. Simply, a dagger crafted from the tooth or claw of a Firstborn. Given freely, fallen, pried from the corpse of some ancient Shadow-Colossus or whatever. Could be a Forsaken or Pure Firstborn, or even one of the briefly mentioned ones in Sundered World or one never mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> The second is similar in vein, and sort of inspired by the HAST/'Ur' write-up in the same day. It occurred to me that we know what omphalos stones are to mages but we don't know what they do for werewolves, if anything (and unofficially, even). Regardless, it's a dagger crafted from a part of a Pangaean's husk, or empowered by (or carved from) an omphalos stone. I'd actually prefer it if the Pangaean was linked to one of the hosts, if possible, even if it's an unofficial one like the Ukusgualu, but any is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the dagger made from a first born's tooth idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:01:26-08:00","id":1184053,"title":"","content":"I'd vote for First Born's tooth and Gauntlet Shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:11:40-08:00","id":1184056,"title":"","content":"Some ideas Per Tribe:<br /> <br /> <u>Blood Talons</u><br /> Wolf Fang: A dagger that does one additional point of damage, it holds the target it strikes or pins him in the case it pierces flesh and also stabs a surface. The target must remove it in order to escape from its pinned place.<br /> <br /> <u>Bone Shadows</u><br /> Wraith Claw: A dagger that makes the prey chill and look around for danger, but without noticing the dagger's bearer, till its too late.<br /> <br /> <u>Iron Masters</u><br /> Niddle tip: A dagger that can never been found upon the bearer no matter how well you search him. It also allows the user to re flexively attack anyone who doesn't know he is armed with the fetish.<br /> <br /> <u>Storm Lords</u><br /> Spark's Edge: A dagger that shocks the target it hits, giving him spasms (aka stun).<br /> <br /> <u>Hunters In Darkness</u><br /> Shard Stabber: A dagger that automatically stabs the shard within a host, if the damage is enough to kill it the rest of its kind within the same body find a horrible death, It works only on hosts that have swarm shard inside them, but not in host monsters. If you give a host monster the final blow with the dager it will do kill the shard within. The knife does not work on shards that have already escaped their hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 02-11-2018, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:40:20-08:00","id":1184063,"title":"","content":"I vote for Gautlet-shard and eclipse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:59:13-08:00","id":1184068,"title":"","content":"As a general matter, I'd love to see something connected to the gauntlet itself and what dwells between and inside. A dagger that cuts the membrane and allows a werewolf to explore (or bad things to escape) would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T14:20:35-08:00","id":1184077,"title":"","content":"I upvoted my favorite option - Pangaean dagger, and encourage others to upvote theirs. The number of Likes is easier to parse than the growing web of crossreferenced posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T14:54:14-08:00","id":1184094,"title":"","content":"2 duplicitous hosts.<br /> 1 azlu and 1 beshilu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:05:40-08:00","id":1184097,"title":"","content":"I am obliged to two answers:<br /> <br /> 1) A gift that now may be a curse from Fox, Vermillion and Wise.<br /> 2) A dagger made from a tooth of Father Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:30:58-08:00","id":1184111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1183975#post1183975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One is inspired by a hint in the Toothcracker's write-up during Five Pounds of Meat. Simply, a dagger crafted from the tooth or claw of a Firstborn. Given freely, fallen, pried from the corpse of some ancient Shadow-Colossus or whatever. Could be a Forsaken or Pure Firstborn, or even one of the briefly mentioned ones in Sundered World or one never mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> The second is similar in vein, and sort of inspired by the HAST/'Ur' write-up in the same day. It occurred to me that we know what omphalos stones are to mages but we don't know what they do for werewolves, if anything (and unofficially, even). Regardless, it's a dagger crafted from a part of a Pangaean's husk, or empowered by (or carved from) an omphalos stone. I'd actually prefer it if the Pangaean was linked to one of the hosts, if possible, even if it's an unofficial one like the Ukusgualu, but any is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love both of these ideas, and am seconding them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:40:24-08:00","id":1184115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1184097#post1184097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am obliged to two answers:<br /> <br /> 1) A gift that now may be a curse from Fox, Vermillion and Wise.<br /> 2) A dagger made from a tooth of Father Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>These would also be awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T16:32:40-08:00","id":1184130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1184097#post1184097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am obliged to two answers:<br /> <br /> 1) A gift that now may be a curse from Fox, Vermillion and Wise.<br /> 2) A dagger made from a tooth of Father Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Number 2 gets my vote","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T18:44:07-08:00","id":1184174,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a shard being made from a part of the Gauntlet, and a blade that can slice the Gauntlet, allowing the user (and possibly others) to enter the vestiges of the Border Marches. These might not be the same blade, and the latter could even be an artifact from the time before the Sundering that had some other effect on the Border Marches before its collapse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T00:52:09-08:00","id":1184283,"title":"","content":"My suggestions are a little less ambitious than a lot of the others in this thread, I guess.<br /> <br /> The first is kind of a last-ditch dagger. A blade that is used on oneself in desperate or hopeless situations as a last resort. What the effect would be, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> The second is a blade used by mortals (or a single mortal) to kill or hunt Uratha. Preferably with some connection to Helios (sun-dipped dagger?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T08:56:45-08:00","id":1184421,"title":"","content":"A dagger that tears a verge between the flesh and shadow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5448-kavagja","name":"Kavagja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T21:14:11-08:00","id":1184610,"title":"","content":"Blade Idigam would be nice. And maybe the tooth blade, as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T03:27:40-08:00","id":1184678,"title":"","content":"I vote for idigam and gauntlet shard","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T05:34:59-08:00","id":1184705,"title":"","content":"<b>Pure Daggers</b><br /> <u>Ivory Claws</u><br /> Liar's Bane: A dagger made for torturing, the user stabs the victim and makes a question, a lie makes the dagger twist inside the wound.<br /> <br /> <u>Fire Touched</u><br /> Bale Cutter: A dagger that where it cuts, bad things inhabiting a body are extracted by force, be it poisons, diseases, spirits etc etc.<br /> <br /> <u>Predator Kings</u><br /> Blade of Prey: A Dagger that never misses its target when thrown, if the user knows the name-taste-smell of the prey, the dagger will literally hunt the target even if in full cover, if the user has seen where the prey took hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 02-11-2018, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:56:56-08:00","id":1185209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1184283#post1184283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestions are a little less ambitious than a lot of the others in this thread, I guess.<br /> <br /> The first is kind of a last-ditch dagger. A blade that is used on oneself in desperate or hopeless situations as a last resort. What the effect would be, I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> The second is a blade used by mortals (or a single mortal) to kill or hunt Uratha. Preferably with some connection to Helios (sun-dipped dagger?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider this my vote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T09:48:06-08:00","id":1185232,"title":"","content":"I'll close the vote some time tomorrow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T06:00:00-08:00","id":1187023,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, vote now closed at last - and I think I've just about figured out which suggestions can be considered to have won the confusing mess that the thread ended up being too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bWill start work soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T10:14:27-08:00","id":1187067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1183967-two-new-daggers?p=1187023#post1187023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so, vote now closed at last - and I think I've just about figured out which suggestions can be considered to have won the confusing mess that the thread ended up being too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bWill start work soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we know what the winners are beforehand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T07:26:34-08:00","id":1187282,"title":"","content":"Time for the first dagger!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i>Zihfurathah</i>, The One Who Separates And Replaces</span></b><br /> It looks like a dagger of the simplest kind \u2013 a short length of bitter sharpness, a grip that fits snugly to the hand, and a way of glinting in the light that seems to reflect not the world around the wielder, but some twisted reflection of grotesque aspect. No-one who has seen the Separator can quite agree on the fine details, though \u2013 what materials it is made out of, if there is a curve to the blade, whether both edges are sharp or just one, what colour the grip is, whether there are any brand markings. This is because the Separator is not simply a knife. Rather, it is a cutting instrument of a unique kind, a tool that has no equivalents in the world beyond itself. It is a concept that does not, yet, fully exist, and so no lexicon can easily categorise it.<br /> <br /> The strange reflections in the blade\u2019s length are the Shadow (or, if the wielder is in the Shadow, the Flesh). If used as a weapon, the keen edge makes the Separator a particularly dangerous knife with a +2L damage rating, but its true power comes in the hands of someone who decides to cut the very world itself. By spending a point of Willpower (or a point of Essence if an Uratha is wielding it), the bearer can focus their concentration and slice a ragged cut through the fabric of the Gauntlet, splitting open the barrier between the two realms so that anyone can cross over through what is essentially a Shadow gateway. A rent cut this way lasts anywhere between 5 turns and 5 hours, after which it will scab over.<br /> <br /> The problem comes in that the scabbed Gauntlet is not just permanently scarred by the injury. The One Who Separates leaves that wound a livid infection. Whenever the Separator is used to slice open a path between worlds, something settles into the Gauntlet through those lacerations. It is not something <i>else</i> exactly, because the dagger is itself a part of something larger, something non-contiguous despite being a coherent whole.<br /> <br /> The dagger appears seemingly at random, discovered or falling into the hands of those who are likely to want to use it. Holding it imparts some sense of its keen edge and its desire to cut away the barriers between realities \u2013 even normal humans can sense this. A werewolf who holds the Separator might think it is a fetish, which is a dangerous mistake to make. The Separator is not caged or controlled at all. If destroyed, the dagger will eventually reform and appear somewhere else, because it is just another limb of The One Who Separates And Replaces, and The One is an <i>idigam</i>.<br /> <br /> The One Who Separates And Replaces is unusual even amongst its mercurial kind, a demonstration that the <i>idigam</i> cannot be easily categorised or predicted. The One is non-contiguous \u2013 it exists in several places and several states at once. The One is Coalesced, but also unCoalesced \u2013 portions of itself have Coalesced, and other parts not, and it is constantly seeking to Coalesce more of itself. Unfortunately, The One Who Separates And Replaces is utterly blasphemous to the order of reality, because it seeks to excise the very Gauntlet and replace that barrier with itself.<br /> <br /> The dagger is its principle tool for expanding itself. Although nothing more than a pseudopod, the dagger represents the partially Coalesced <i>idigam</i>\u2019s drive to cut away the Gauntlet \u2013 which it considers, like a calculating surgeon, to be necrotic and dead matter that must be replaced with something fresh and new. Because nothing exists that could perform such a task, the Separator was created as an entirely new concept, but the <i>idigam</i> is not yet capable of propagating that concept throughout reality \u2013 only the areas it directly influences or manifests.<br /> <br /> Wherever the Seperator wounds the Gauntlet, the One Who Separates begins to infect and overwrite it, carving and slicing the Gauntlet-concept away to be replaced by the <i>idigam</i>. The <i>idigam-</i>barrier will infect an area around the puncture of up to five hundred yards, spreading one yard per day. After it reaches five hundred yards, the infection slows to one yard per year, unless another spreading area is within five miles, in which case it continues to spread one yard per day until it has connected to the other area. Corrupted Gauntlet can theoretically be destroyed by using the <i>idigam</i>\u2019s Bane, but while the One Who Replaces is Coalesced where it replaces the Gauntlet, the bulk of its self is still Uncoalesced, and so it has not yet manifested a stable Bane \u2013 instead, every portion of its barrier-self has the same cycling Bane and Ban as the unCoalesced part does. Where its infection is excised, the One is replaced by a fresh membrane of Gauntlet at its weakest, which will slowly adjust towards its appropriate strength over the course of several decades.<br /> <br /> The unCoalesced idigam moves around erratically through the Shadow, little more than an afterthought of its activities in cutting away and replacing the Gauntlet. Eventually, once more than five hundred square miles of Gauntlet has been replaced by the One Who Replaces, there will be more of its spiritual essence in its Coalesced form than its unCoalesced, whereupon it will manifest a stable Bane.<br /> <br /> Where The One Who Separates has replaced the Gauntlet, it changes the nature of what the Gauntlet is and does in order to suit its own desires for how the barrier between worlds should behave. While the two worlds remain physically separate, any sharp edge can be used, along with a Willpower point, to cut an aperture between them that will last for five rounds. Additionally, the Gauntlet-replacement is permeable to shed blood, spilled viscera, the wind, marble, sounds of crying, and mathematical division; these concepts will propagate from one side to the other as if the barrier were not there so that, for example, half the blood from an injury would be appearing out of no-where on the other side of the Gauntlet, a marble pillar will be an obstacle in both worlds, and someone performing mathematical division in their mind would find the ideas simply leaking out of their confused thoughts across the Gauntlet to appear directly as Resonance on the other side. It remains possible for some beings, such as werewolves, to see across the Gauntlet and into the other world, but the other four senses are unable to extend across; attempting to do so instead triggers tiny lacerations to the sinuses, tongue, ears, etc., dealing one point of lethal damage in the process. Any ghost that forms in the area under the false-Gauntlet is immediately dragged through into the Shadow. Any character attempting to infiltrate or add themselves to a social structure that they have damaged or that they have killed a member of will benefit from the rote action on any rolls to do so. Any Resonance of hope or fear burns on contact with the false-Gauntlet, choking the Shadow off from those concepts and preventing humans from recovering any Willpower due to Vices or Virtues that match those emotions. Finally, creatures on the Flesh side of the false-Gauntlet regain an additional point of Willpower whenever they cut apart, flay, flense or mangle another creature extensively, whether living or dead \u2013 so a human cutting a chicken carcass apart at home will feel a strange rush, the same rush as when they cut their neighbour apart.<br /> <br /> There is one other form that The One Who Replaces takes \u2013 that of Essence itself. If the Seperator is plunged into the anchor of a locus, or a locus falls under the influence of the false-Gauntlet area, it becomes tainted by The One Who Replaces in Essence form. Anyone partaking of the Essence finds it has a Resonance of cutting-things-away-from-other-things-and-thus-transforming-them. It functions as normal Essence in most ways, but a creature who has even a single point of it in their Essence pool is slowly cut apart, slices of skin and flesh or ephemera flensed away in carefully measured pieces. At first, this damage comes at one point of Lethal per hour, but after five hours, it increases to one point of Lethal per minute, and after five days (if the victim survives that long and doesn\u2019t purge the Essence from themselves) it increases to one point of Lethal per turn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The One Who Separates And Replaces</b></span><br /> Rank 5 unCoalesced idigam<br /> Power 14 Finesse 13 Resistance 15<br /> Willpower 10 Essence 100 Initiative 28 Defence 13 Speed 27 Size 15 Corpus 30<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast, Dement, Drain, Entropic Decay, Ghost Eater, Implant Mission, Regenerate<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Reaching, Gauntlet Breach, Shadow Gateway, Materialize, Image<br /> <b>Essence Shaping: </b>Gauntlet Manipulation<br /> <b>Dread Power:</b> Shifting<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Changes every scene.<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Changes every scene.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The One Who Separates And Replaces</b></span><br /> Rank 6 Coalesced idigam<br /> As a Rank 6 being, the Coalesced form of The One Who Separates And Replaces is beyond representation through attribute numbers. It is also extremely unusual for an <i>idigam</i> in that its chrysalis is taking place as its actual Coalescence \u2013 The One has already identified the question it wishes to be the answer to, and is answering it via its Coalescence process. As it is turning itself into a replacement for the Gauntlet itself, it is essentially a phenomenon rather than an entity, and can only be damaged and removed through its Ban and Bane \u2013 whatever those will turn out to be.<br /> <br /> Once The One covers up to five thousand square miles with itself, it will be fully Coalesced, and will no longer require its Essence or dagger forms. At that point, The One Who Separates And Replaces will only exist as an invasive Gauntlet-replacement, and will begin to naturally spread at a rate of one mile per day until it covers the entirety of the Shadow within the Warden Moon\u2019s stride.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T08:07:47-08:00","id":1187288,"title":"","content":"What about those poor things that live within the Gauntlet? Do they just die or mutate and change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T08:19:34-08:00","id":1187291,"title":"","content":"That's a really inventive and interesting Idigam, damn. It reminds me a little of some of the nastier Horrors in Earthdawn, who constituted phenomena that perverted the plane of magic itself, rather than &quot;merely&quot; being creatures with twisted patterns and magic or life-corrupting powers. The way The One's various manifestations are linked and what they're building up to are quite evocative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T09:16:20-08:00","id":1187300,"title":"","content":"Is there adverse effects to crossing the gauntlet w