transforming-them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is what I call a eureka moment. <br /> <br /> But what about wind and crying?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T02:15:31-08:00","id":1187496,"title":"","content":"Injuries make you cry. This might be why the Idigam removes hope and fear - to encourage acceptance of transformation.<br /> <br /> The wind is an outlier, and may be related to circumstances of Idigams (partial) Coalescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T12:48:18-08:00","id":1187625,"title":"","content":"Well, the concept of &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RazorWind\" target=\"_blank\">razor wind</a>&quot; is a thing, after all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T17:40:14-08:00","id":1187698,"title":"","content":"Be careful with those TVtropes links, those can take hours out of your day, roaming from page to page.<br /> <br /> But back on topic, I always enjoy new ways to screw with the gauntlet, and Zihfurathah is a particularly impressive one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T09:51:13-08:00","id":1188552,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Hekatonchiere\u2019s Sliver</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">They planned to murder a god, which is never a simple task. They believed it was the right thing to do, for themselves and all the world. A sense of righteousness isn\u2019t enough to handle deicide (never mind patricide), though, no matter how delusionally strong the belief may be. Bringing down the Great Predator would require every ounce of strength and cleverness they could bring together \u2013 the greatest hunt ever perpetrated, even if performed with deep grief in their hearts and tears in their eyes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">They went to the Hekatonchiere, that vast and writhing god that undulated across the landscape of the Pangaean paradise. Did they hunt the great and worming horror as it marched on its fractal confusion of hands, and crack its soul apart for the blade they sought? Or did they gather beneath one of its fifty bulging heads, each dribbling a rain of venomous fangs down, and while enduring those sacred venoms petition the ancient one for its aid? When they returned, they bore the sliver, and prepared to sheathe it in the body and soul of their ultimate prey.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Almost nothing of the Hekatonchiere\u2019s Sliver is known to the Uratha of today, let alone how the Uratha of the distant past acquired it, or whether they actually managed to use it. Today, it is a lethal gift, an endowment passed from one champion to another. The sliver is a long, thin weapon, almost like a stiletto yet with a keen edge as well as pricking point. There is no separation of blade, handle or grip; the whole thing is a single, seamless piece of a substance somewhere between bone and basalt. It doesn\u2019t look like it was originally designed to be gripped at all, one end just worn with indentations from centuries, even millennia, of handling. The substance is harder than diamond, seemingly near-unbreakable by mundane means, but is porous; some of the holes towards the base are nearly a quarter of an inch wide. It feels slightly greasy to the touch.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Simply used as a weapon, the Sliver is malevolent enough. By spending a point of Essence upon striking a living foe, an Uratha wielding the sliver can inflict the grave Poisoned Tilt on the victim; when the scene ends, so does the Tilt, but the poison then continues to ravage the victim\u2019s flesh every hour for a day, with a Toxicity equal to the Uratha\u2019s Primal Urge. The poison manifests as a blackening and thickening of the blood, soon resulting in the growth of pustules that burst to reveal new-born centipedes writhing in the ichor, and a shifting beneath the victim\u2019s skin as many-legged threads twitch and squirm in their veins. If the victim dies, their body discorporates into nothing more than a bag of sickly skin and bones containing a thrashing mass of centipedes of all manner of species, which quickly erupt from their container and scatter with no cohesion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If driven into a Host, or other body-hopping entity, the venom sticks to the Shard or entity, not the flesh \u2013 so if the creature abandons its current form, the venom will continue to plague it in whatever new form it takes or acquires until the duration is run.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The true potential of the Hekatonchiere\u2019s Sliver requires a more intimate binding between Uratha and fragment. It is done directly enough \u2013 a bizarre mimicry of the sword-swallower\u2019s art. The would-be user tilts their head back and pushes the sliver down their open throat, into their guts. This is not a clean or cleverly bloodless operation \u2013 the Uratha intentionally drives the Sliver into the meat and tissues of their own innards, pushing until it is entirely enclosed within their flesh. This deals 3 points of lethal damage to the Uratha (or 3 points of aggravated damage to anyone else stupid enough to try it, and for whom no further benefits will occur regardless) and is agonisingly painful.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once swallowed and made one with the Uratha\u2019s internals, the Sliver undergoes a transformation. It twists and writhes, made suddenly pliable, and a myriad of prickling legs exude from its substance. Animated, it coils and nestles into the bloodied viscera; in return, those self-same internal tissues thread into its pores \u2013 strings of gristle and organ that themselves twitch and shudder on little limbs of cartilage, an invasion of the invader, an intimate embrace on the inside. So bound, the Sliver and Uratha are one. Removing the Sliver will kill the Uratha, literally ripping the werewolf\u2019s Essence and spirit from their flesh. If the Uratha perishes while the Sliver nests within them, their corpse is immediately reduced to a mass of writhing centipedes and a pile of picked-clean bones, the Hekatonchiere\u2019s Sliver reverted to its long, piercing point and lying amongst the noisome mess.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Sliver-bound Uratha bears a number of significant benefits. Firstly, their jaws and claws take on the sliver\u2019s porous, oddly stony appearance, and they can trigger the Sliver\u2019s poisonous effects on any attack they make with their natural weaponry for the normal Essence cost. Secondly, whenever the Uratha suffers the Poisoned Tilt, they may choose to immediately end it \u2013 and furthermore gain a single point of Essence from doing so.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">By spending 2 Essence, the Uratha may vomit forth a stream of poisonous centipedes, spraying an area of up to fifteen feet in front of them with the toxic creatures. Victims struck by the mass of centipedes must pass a Stamina roll with a -2 penalty or gain the moderate Poisoned Tilt; furthermore, the centipedes remain in the area for the scene, biting and attacking anything that steps within the area and thus forcing further such rolls against creatures unfortunate enough to remain in or entire their swarm.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Several of the Uratha\u2019s forms mutate and change, featuring disturbing additions of arthropod aspect. In Dalu, the Uratha\u2019s hands and feet can cling to walls and they can therefore climb even sheer surfaces with trivial ease. The same is true in Gauru form, and the Uratha additionally receives an extra point of armour in that form. In Urshul, the Uratha receives the extra point of armour, and furthermore the form has at least one additional pair of legs (and likely a distended, longer body than normal), adding a +3 bonus to attempts to remain stable or resist being knocked over. Only Hishu and Urhan remain untouched by the Sliver\u2019s influence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Finally, the Uratha possesses perfect awareness of all centipedes within thirty-three yards, can command centipedes with the First Tongue, may apply the rote action rules to a single Strength-based dice pool once per scene, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">and once per scene may turn into a fractal concept capable of applying a single action (other than an attack) to every viable target of that action in the scene, such as opening every door with a single turn of their hand regardless of distance to that door, or of crushing every insect underfoot with a single stamp, etc. etc.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bonding with the Hekatonchiere\u2019s Sliver is a slow death sentence. The bonded Uratha has thirty three years to live, after which the Sliver rips their spirit away and they perish, their corpse mulching into a mass of writhing centipedes. Due to this limitation, the Sliver is usually passed to Uratha who do not expect to survive the full thirty-three years anyway, and who can therefore exploit its powers as fully as possible without fear of mortality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There are hints that the Sliver can do more, or once had more power. Some tales suggest the dagger-bonded could turn into a massive, carapaced horror that puts the killing form to shame, or that past wielders were able to fundamentally change the nature of venoms in the vicinity in ways that mocked the laws of physics, causing poisons to kill relationships, or weaken gravity, or to spread to whoever spoke a poisoned victim\u2019s name aloud. A few stories have it that the bonded gained great ability to shape and reform matter, tearing boulders apart with ease and rendering impossible, Escheresque structures from the resulting rubble. It\u2019s not clear to what extent these claims are fabricated or exaggerated stories, or whether a modern wielder could achieve the same things. However, at least one recent bonded reported gaining a sense of the limbs of other living beings within a wide radius \u2013 possibly thirty-three miles, and a limited ability to influence or even briefly possess the hands of humans who they concentrated on, forcing the victims\u2019 limbs to move in accordance with the Uratha\u2019s wishes rather than those of their horrified owners.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T09:56:38-08:00","id":1188555,"title":"","content":"Freaking sweet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T10:04:48-08:00","id":1188558,"title":"","content":"Centipede, Venomous and Terrifying?<br /> <br /> Good stuff, by the way. I must wonder if the Silver is in fact a form of &quot;spirit shard&quot;, and the creation of the new centipedes is how it tries to generate new Shards, but without success. Maybe there are other Silvers like it around the world, or perhaps some true Centipede Hosts are actually out there, and they search for the lost part of their god, which they claim to be rightfully theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T10:27:28-08:00","id":1188561,"title":"","content":"Hmm... seems like it would be a Rank 4 Pangaean. Fox (Rank 5) has the whole 333 miles and Bane of a weapon made from 333 foxes thing going on, while Harvest has 44 miles and an amulet inscribed with the names of 44 people who died from starvation as a Bane. Factors of ten, perhaps? Rank 3 have numerical patterns in the ones, Rank 4 in the tens, Rank 5 in the hundreds, Rank 6 in the thousands, Rank 7 in the ten thousands, and Rank 8 in the hundred thousands? Hmm... with Wolf as Rank 8 that would give them a sensory radius wide enough to interplay with the Moon, which makes a lot of sense. Rank 6 is global reach already, potentially, and Rank 7 is up into the atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd probably give Centipede (the Hekatoncheire?) the Space Arcanum. Fractals and manipulating things at range. Poisons that ruin relationships, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://f